# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# Every client-side route in this app (/feed, /profile/me, /explore, ...) is
# handled by the React router, not by a file on disk. Without this rule a hard
# refresh or a shared deep link such as
#   https://app.echoflow.in/?clip=42
# asks Pages for a path that does not exist and gets a 404 before React ever
# boots. The trailing `200` makes Pages serve index.html for any unmatched
# path while leaving the URL intact, so the router can read the query string.
#
# `/*` (not `/*  /index.html  200` with spaces) — Pages copies this file
# verbatim from public/ into the build output; it is not processed.
#
# Real files (assets under /assets/, /index.html, /_headers, icons) are
# matched BEFORE this rule, so hashed JS/CSS bundles are still served with
# their long cache headers and are not swallowed by the fallback.
/*    /index.html   200
